; The sky. Every number in the *look* of it lives in the shader's own uniform
; defaults rather than being overridden here, so there is one file to open when
; the weather is wrong — see res://src/world/sky.gdshader, which also carries
; the renderer note about why it is a single full-res pass.
;
; The one exception is below, and it is an exception because it is not a fact
; about weather: where the sun stands is a fact about this driveway, the same
; kind of thing as the Key light's transform a few lines down, and it belongs in
; the room rather than in the paint. It is also the number that has to be
; readable without a rendering device — the shader's own defaults are not, which
; tests/integration/test_garage.gd found the hard way.
[sub_resource type="ShaderMaterial" id="ShaderMaterial_sky"]
shader = ExtResource("4_sky")
shader_parameter/sun_direction = Vector3(0.45, 0.56, 0.7)

; PROCESS_MODE_INCREMENTAL and the smallest radiance map going, because with
; reflections off below neither one is feeding anything: this keeps the engine
; from spending a cubemap bake per frame on a sky nothing samples.
[sub_resource type="Sky" id="Sky_driveway"]
sky_material = SubResource("ShaderMaterial_sky")
process_mode = 2
radiance_size = 0

; background_mode 2 is BG_SKY. The two lines under `sky` are the deliberate
; part, and both are decisions rather than defaults:
;
;   ambient_light_source = 2 is AMBIENT_SOURCE_COLOR — the grey that was tuned
;   against the flat backdrop, kept. Switching it to 3 (SKY) would hand the
;   ambient over to the sky, which is a nicer-sounding sentence than it is a
;   picture: it tints the whole car and the grass blue and every value the two
;   strip lights were balanced at has to be found again. That is a relight, and
;   a relight is its own change.
;
;   reflected_light_source = 1 is REFLECTION_SOURCE_DISABLED, and it is doing
;   real work — the default (0, BG) would start mirroring this sky the moment
;   the background became one. The power wash is the only metal in the game at
;   metallic 0.9 / roughness 0.25, and it is meant to read as dark metal with
;   hard highlights.
;
;   Rendered both ways rather than argued about. With this at 2 the wand in the
;   viewmodel goes pale blue chrome end to end, its one hard highlight replaced
;   by a mirrored sky, and the mud on the car lifts and desaturates with it —
;   the red paint showing through a half-washed panel stops reading as paint.
;   It is one line to look at it yourself, and it is worth looking at once; the
;   cost is that plus a cubemap bake. src/world/view_model.gd's class docs carry
;   the same note.
[sub_resource type="Environment" id="Environment_bay"]
background_mode = 2
sky = SubResource("Sky_driveway")
ambient_light_source = 2
ambient_light_color = Color(0.48, 0.5, 0.56, 1)
ambient_light_energy = 0.9
reflected_light_source = 1

